    "evidence_text": " Formerly, she was the President of The Home Depot Canada and the Home Depot Asia, overseeing the growth of the company's Canadian operations from 19 to 179 stores between 1996 and 2011.\n\n She also led The Home Depot's entry into China.\n\nRon Brill\n\nRonald M. Brill is a former American retail executive and is a co-founder of the Home Depot.\n\n Brill was Home Depot's 1st official employee.\n\n He worked with Home Depot for over 20 years, serving as the company's Chief Administration Officer from 1995-2000.\n\nFrank Blake\n\nFrancis Stanton \"Frank\" Blake (born July 30, 1949) is an American businessman and lawyer, who was the chairman and CEO of The Home Depot from January 2007 to May 2014.\n\n He was a longtime prot\u00e9g\u00e9 of Robert Nardelli.\n\n Longtime prot\u00e9g\u00e9 Denise Morrison, who worked for him at Nabisco as well as Campbell's, succeeded him as CEO.\n\nFrank Blake (American football)\n\n He had earlier served in a similar capacity at The Home Depot from December 2000 to January 2007.",
